    "result_text": "All green. Let me summarize what was done.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so the `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, and every value derived from it now reflects that new identity. The full build passes (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS`), and the audit log confirms the new format in practice (`customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`).\n\n### Changes\n\n1. **`AssignCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 rewrote the step. It no longer counts existing owners or uses sequence numbers (dropped `OwnerRepository`). It now builds `REGION + \"-\" + HASH8`:\n   - **REGION** = region derived from the postcode via the new `Locality.regionOf(postcode)` (NSW/VIC/QLD, else `UNKNOWN`).\n   - **HASH8** = first 8 upper-case hex characters of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName`. The telephone is already E.164-normalized by the time this step runs (normalized in `ValidateOwnerFields`, mapped in `BuildOwner`).\n\n2. **`Locality.java`** \u2014 added `regionOf(String postcode)` (postcode-only region, no city fallback \u2014 the REGION segment of the code) and `of(Owner owner)`, which reads locality from the `customerCode`'s REGION segment, falling back to the old city/postcode derivation only for records with no customer code (e.g. seed data).\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 `locality` now maps via `Locality.of(owner)`, moving it onto the new region-and-hash identity.\n\n4. **Values that moved automatically** (they already read `customerCode`, no code change needed, verified by tests/logs):\n   - **membershipNumber** (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`) \u2192 now `NSW-1A2B3C4D-M26` shape.\n   - **checkDigit** \u2014 Luhn over the digits now present in the new code.\n   - **create audit record** (`AuditOwnerCreated`) \u2014 logs the new `customerCode`.\n\n5. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, and `locality` descriptions/examples to document the new identity.\n\nThe redesign is deterministic: the same telephone + last name in the same region always produce the same `customerCode`, with no sequence numbers anywhere.",
